  "worked_solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & k & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|-k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|+k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(3\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 0)-k(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 4)+k(0\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =15+8k-12k \\\\  & =15-4k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 15-4k & =0 \\\\ 4k & =15 \\\\ k & =\\frac{15}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{15}{4}.$",
